---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Terms | GurtOS at Cal Hacks 13.0" description="Terms for the GurtOS Cal Hacks showcase: a hackathon showcase of open-source software, provided as is.">
  <article class="wrap legal">
    <p class="kicker">Terms</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lead">This site is a showcase of GurtOS, an open-source project built by one person for the Cal Hacks 13.0 hackathon. By using it you agree to these plain terms.</p>

    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      The pages describe a hackathon project and the evidence for it. It is a preview, not a product, and nothing here is an
      offer to sell or support anything. Parts of the project are labelled live, test or simulated on each page. Believe the
      labels.
    </p>

    <h2>The software</h2>
    <p>
      GurtOS is licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and its source is at <a href={LINKS.repo}>github.com/benz16107/calhacks13</a>.
      The license, not these terms, governs what you may do with the code and the install discs. The discs are an early
      preview: verify their signatures, run them on a machine you can wipe, and do not use them for anything that matters.
      The software comes without warranty, as the license says.
    </p>

    <h2>Test money, test data</h2>
    <p>
      Every payment shown is test money: Stripe test mode, a Visa test card, or USDC on Solana devnet. The companies, people
      and customers in the demos are made up, and the credit and bank data come from sponsors' sandboxes. Nothing here is
      financial, legal, security or compliance advice. The sample letters and rules are models for a demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Names and trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      Sponsor, product and company names belong to their owners. They are used only to say which prize track a page is for
      and which service the project talks to. Their use is no endorsement by, or partnership with, those companies.
    </p>

    <h2>Links and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Links to other sites are for convenience, and we do not control them. We may change or remove pages at any time, for
      example to fix a wrong fact.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty, no liability</h2>
    <p>
      The site and the software are provided as is, without warranty of any kind. To the extent the law allows, the author is
      not liable for any loss from using them.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>To ask about these terms, open an issue in the project's <a href={LINKS.repo}>GitHub repository</a>.</p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated Oct 24, 2026.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .legal .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-focus);
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
